<title>UK: Brit.Energy to confirm cost cuts - paper.</title>
<headline>Brit.Energy to confirm cost cuts - paper.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-10-06</dateline>
<text>
<p>British Energy, the privatised nuclear power generator, will confirm this week a 100 million stg cost-cutting pprogramme that will mean shedding up to a quarter of its workforce by the end of the decade, said the Observer newspaper.</p>
<p>A total of some 1,500 jobs will go from its eight nuclear power plants, raising fears about safety, the article said.</p>
<p>Insiders say the company plans to cut its present staffing levels of between 450 and 600 per reactor to about 375 per reactor and the trade unions are preparing for an announcement on Tuesday, it said.</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44 171 542 7717</p>
